From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Nikolajs Agafonovs <nikolajs.agafonovs@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 16:06:05 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] i386: code size: relaxation in functions with inline asm,
 mapped targets in its iteration, jumps to the next instruction removed, a
 local reloaded right after its store taken from the register, 16-bit absolute
 addresses with -m16

The kernel's real-mode setup with its video mode code was 1200 bytes
over the 32 KB of the boot protocol (_end 0x84b0 against setup.ld's
0x8000) with the code-size pass of the previous commit; it is 1136
bytes under now (0x7b90), so kernel patch 0011 (X86_BOOT_VIDEO_MODES)
can go.

 * relax_function() no longer gives up on a function with an asm
   statement: the assembler's forward references leave relocations and
   symbols, which are patched like the compiler's own.  What would go
   wrong is an address of the function's section that the assembler
   folds into the code -- a displacement to a label it has already
   defined (asm_local_sym_here()), the difference of two labels
   (asm_expr_sum(), asm_pass_resolve()), .org -- or an alignment in it:
   tccasm.c and i386-asm.c report those with gen_relax_asm_fixed() and
   such a function is left alone.  func_asm_seen is gone.  A local
   label of such a function keeps its symbol until the end of the file
   (gen_relax_active(), asked by asm_fixup_local_label_relocs()), so
   that relaxation moves it like any symbol; converted at once, its
   address would sit in the in-place addend of a section-relative
   relocation, which the kernel's `.long 1b - .` exception-table
   entries showed: a first version patched such addends and misjudged
   them by the 4 bytes of a jump displacement, and the i386 kernel died
   on its first expected fault in copy_to_kernel_nofault().
 * The fixed-point iteration mapped nothing: gen_relax_map() is the
   identity while relax_saved is 0, so a backward jump was measured
   against its unmapped target, looked shorter than it would be, and the
   final check then dropped the relaxation of the whole function
   (vsprintf, display_menu, __cmdline_find_option, raw_set_mode in the
   setup).  relax_saved is set during the iteration; a jmp to the next
   instruction is removed (nlen 0).
 * load() of a local that the instruction(s) just emitted stored a
   register to (`x = e; ... x ...`, a spilled value used at once, the
   saves of the regparm prologue) emits nothing when that register is
   the one wanted, else a mov/movzx/movsx from it (3 bytes instead of 5
   with -m16); a narrower load at the same offset is served by a wider
   store.  store() notes the stores emitted since the last other
   instruction (st_notes[]); a label (gind(), gsym_addr() at ind), an
   asm statement and the next function's prologue forget them
   (gen_sync()).  A narrower load into the register that holds the slot
   (`r == (signed char)r` with r just stored, tcc's own gjmp_addr())
   narrows the note to those bytes: the first version kept it whole, the
   full-width load of r that followed was taken from the extended byte,
   every backward jump of the self-compiled tcc looked short, and test3
   of the guest's suite crashed while tests2 and the cross-compiled
   tests passed.
 * gen_modrm() with -m16 encodes an absolute address in the 16-bit form
   (modrm 0x06, an R_386_16 relocation), as GNU as does for .code16gcc,
   instead of 0x67 with a 32-bit one: 3 bytes less per global access.
   Such code is linked below 64 KB (the setup, the real-mode
   trampoline); tld reports an overflow.

The setup with the video mode code, i386-tcc -m16, _end: 0x84b0 ->
0x8120 (relaxation with asm, reloads) -> 0x7b90 (mapped targets, 16-bit
addresses); gcc -Os gives 0x4e80.  make test passes, tests/m16-check.sh
codegen finds the -m16 and -m32 streams of the boot objects identical.
---
 i386-asm.c |   4 +-
 i386-gen.c | 185 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++------
 tcc.h      |   7 +-
 tccasm.c   |  12 ++++
 tccgen.c   |   4 +-
 5 files changed, 187 insertions(+), 25 deletions(-)

diff --git a/i386-asm.c b/i386-asm.c
index b54c3d0..5774cd7 100644
--- a/i386-asm.c
+++ b/i386-asm.c
@@ -676,8 +676,10 @@ static ElfSym *asm_local_sym_here(Sym *sym)
 {
     ElfSym *esym = elfsym(sym);
     if (esym && esym->st_shndx == cur_text_section->sh_num
-        && ELFW(ST_BIND)(esym->st_info) == STB_LOCAL)
+        && ELFW(ST_BIND)(esym->st_info) == STB_LOCAL) {
+        gen_relax_asm_fixed(esym->st_shndx); /* its address is folded in */
         return esym;
+    }
     return NULL;
